Gnomebog, a wiry gnome with a penchant for mischief, found himself in Stranglethorn Vale, clutching a well-worn, yet surprisingly robust, succubus named Lys. Unlike the flashy voidwalkers, Lys was practical—helping Gnomebog through mud, thorns, and the occasional angry troll. One day, Gnomebog stumbled upon a hidden gnomish ritual site, where a cryptic totem instructed, “Choose the shadow that guides, not the one that dazzles.” It turned out the totem was a trick: the ritual actually made succubi more appealing to new warlocks, as their utility in rough terrain (healing, buffs, crowd control) made them surprisingly popular despite old stereotypes. Gnomebog’s story proved it: succubi were the real workhorses, and the riddle’s answer was simple—**the succubus’ utility in real-world play made them more common than people thought.** [end of text]


